  - name: IOWait Max
    detail: Minimum IOWait has exceeded a 25% CPU threshold for over 5 mins
    calendar: OfficeHours
    fluxfile: flux/usage_iowait.flux
    severity: 1
    threshold: 25 
    comparison: gt
    tags: 
      - host
      - _field
      - _measurement
    interval: 300
    target: postfix
    action: | 
              An extended period of extremely high I/O during normal working hours indicates unusal activity, a defective process or
              a problem with underlying storage. The BPSA dashboard can indicate problems on the Netapp storage. VM metrics can be
              used to ascertain if there is a sudden and unusal spike in disk activity. Login and use iotop and iostat to find
              the process and storage volume affected. I/O wait may also occur on network connections. Check on the health
              of the database servers. Use the Azure portal to look for any events associated with the resource affected. 
